# This is a file of tests for the GMOS sequencer in a suitable format to be read
# by the tcsTests.tk procedure.
# 
# This particular test file is aimed at checking the input ranges to 
# the GMOS 'dtaPos' CAD command.
#
#
# Comments are introduced by a # in the first column
# Blank lines can be left if required.
# The currently allowed keywords are (case is immaterial)
#
#  Test   <testId>
#  Command <commandName>
#  Field   <CAD field> <value>
#  Response Accept | Reject
#  Timeout <msecs>
#  OnError Continue | Abort
#  Log     <recordName>
#  Directive Start | Preset

# This first part before the first Test keyword can be used to setup 
# global values for Response, TimeOut and OnError. These global values
# can be over ridden within specific tests

Response Reject
TimeOut  30000
OnError  Continue

Help
Help These tests checks the trapping of invalid input to the
Help dtaPos command.
Help
Help The first tests check for null input. If the commands in question have
Help been run at any time after booting and prior to running these tests then
Help there will already be input on the CAD fields and so these null tests
Help will fail. To validate the trapping of null input you will have to
Help reboot the GMOS sequencer and start these tests again.
Help
Help Press continue when ready
Help

# Tests start here. Each test must start with the Test keyword, end with
# a Directive keyword and have at least one Command keyword. Any Field
# keywords are assumed to apply to the last command

Test UT06010
Summary Check rejection of null input
Help Check rejection of null input

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  DIR MARK   
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start
 
Test UT06015
Summary Check rejection of null input to Y and Z-axis position fields
Help Check rejection of null input to Y and Z-axis position fields

 Command dtaPos
 Field  A   1.0
 Field  DIR MARK   
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06020
Summary Check rejection of null input to Z-axis position field
Help Check rejection of null input to X-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  1.0
 Field  B  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06030
Summary Check rejection of invalid input to X-axis position field
Help Check rejection of invalid input to X-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  XXXX
 Field  B  1.0
 Field  C  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06040
Summary Check rejection of invalid input to Y-axis position field
Help Check rejection of invalid input to Y-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  1.0
 Field  B  XXXX
 Field  C  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06050
Summary Check rejection of invalid input to Z-axis position field
Help Check rejection of invalid input to Z-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  1.0
 Field  B  1.0
 Field  C  XXXX
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06060
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to X-axis position field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to X-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  300.0
 Field  B  1.0
 Field  C  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06070
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Y-axis position field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Y-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  1.0
 Field  B  300.0
 Field  C  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06080
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Z-axis position field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Z-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  1.0
 Field  B  1.0
 Field  C  300.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06090
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to X-axis position field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to X-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  -100.0
 Field  B  1.0
 Field  C  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06100
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Y-axis position field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Y-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  1.0
 Field  B  -100.0
 Field  C  1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06110
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Z-axis position field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Z-axis position field

 Command dtaPos 
 Field  A  100.0
 Field  B  100.0
 Field  C  -1.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT06120
Summary Check acceptance of valid positions
Summary Check acceptance of valid positions

  Aftertest Pause

  Log c2:dtaAssembly.A
  Log c2:dtaAssembly.B
  Log c2:dtaAssembly.C

 Command dtaPos 
  Field  A  100.0
  Field  B  200.0
  Field  C  300.0
  Response  Accept
  Directive Start
  
# Test UT06130
# Summary Check that rejection by Components Controller is reported correctly
# NO TEST AVAILABLE
#

